From 1a5641283f89c25bc0312f91c3318435a78652c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:36:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Discover's sections held and moved, a tick at the lift
 and a click at each place (build 95 note 9)

His word, 2026-11-13: "allow the user to hold down each section and the
haptic feedback hits and they can move each section according to their
wants (and every time it switches a section a haptic feedback hits)".

A resting finger lifts a band after the house's hold (400 ms, a verse's
own): it grows 3% with its shadow faded in, and one light tick is felt.
Drawn, it follows the finger; the bands it passes step aside on the house
curve, each giving way once the held band covers half of it (6px of slack,
so a trembling finger flicks nothing), with one click per change of place
(the chapter strip's own) and none between. Near the top bar or the tab bar
the page scrolls with it. Let go, it settles where it was shown and the
order is drawn in the same frame, kept on the device. A tap still opens a
band and a swipe still scrolls.

Without a drag (WCAG 2.5.7): Arrange sections, under the list, opens the
house's sheet with Move up and Move down per band (Your rule's words), each
move said aloud and felt as one click, the keyboard kept on the band it
moved, and Restore the original order at its foot once the order is the
reader's own. Reduced motion: the band follows the finger and nothing
else travels. The clicks follow Settings, Clicks as you scroll. On the
website a page loaded whole shows the kept order from its first paint
(a pre-paint script with the request's nonce); in the apps every visit is
the router's, which reads the order before the first draw.

lib/discover/holdToMove.ts decides (a pure machine), lib/discover/
doorOrder.ts keeps, components/discover/DoorOrder.tsx and ArrangeSheet.tsx
draw. Five new words in all 21 languages. 46 tests in three new files, all
failing on the old code.

